1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Han kalles ofte Stee fordi han drev gården til stesønnen kunne overta. Han kjøpte og arvet en rekke parter i nordre og sørre egge fra 1650 og utover. Han eide etter hvert 15 skinn i Nordre egge og 6 skinn i sørre. 
2 CONC Sønnen Nils overtok hele godset 
2 CONT
2 CONT Han og Lokrits hadde 3 barn som vi vet om:
2 CONT
2 CONT *Nils 1648-1729 på Egge, 
2 CONT *Ola, og 
2 CONT *Sebjør gm Johannes Knutsen Hjelle
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT He may have come from Skeager in Land.  On page 437 of the bygdebok it mentions that he had some connection with Ole Engebretsen there.  In the 1664 census, Ole Engebretsen is at Nedre Skeager, Land and he is 67, which would have 
2 CONC been too young to have been Ole Olsen's father, unless his father was 15 when he was born or the ages are listed incorrectly.
2 CONT
2 CONT His son, Niels Olsen, is NOT listed in the 1664 census
2 CONT
2 CONT See Østinni bygdebok page 159
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT He may have come from Skeager in Land, Oppland.  On page 437 of the Vestre Slidre bygdebok it mentions that he had some connection with Ole Engebretsen there.  In the 1664 census, Ole Engebretsen is at Nedre Skeager, Land and he i
2 CONC s 67, which would have been too young to have been Ole Olsen's father, unless his father was 15 when he was born or the ages are listed incorrectly.  See also the Østinni bygdebok page 159, he is referenced there.
