2 CONT Far til Henrik Henriksen Blank Våga som var lensmann i Vikedal var Henrik Blank fra Skottland, f. 1560 og gift med Anna Olafsdatter Nesheim
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Henrik was the lensmann in Vikedal from 1626 until 1654.  He leased
2 CONT the farm Våga in Imsland, which was owned by the King, from 1611 until
2 CONT he died.
2 CONT Henrik, the son of the rich Henrik Blank and descended from the Losna
2 CONT family, owned property worth about 12 laup smør in 1634.  But by his death around 1658, he owned an estate valued at 20 laupar smør.  On 26 April 1619, Henrik received a document from the provincial governor granting him the right
2 CONC  to establis h a sawmill at Våga.  For this privilege he paid the King 10 riksdalar and two dozen wooden planks per year.  Henrik fell ill in 1655 and probably died around 1658.
