1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Lindanger i Tysvær Rogaland; Jfr g og folk bok 4 s462
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 2420. Ola Holgerson SKIFTUN/LINDANGER (1028) (1029) was born in 1600 in Skiftun, Hjelmeland, Rogaland, Norway. He died in 1660. Ola lived first at Skiftun in Hjelmeland. There he was farm owner in association with his uncle Sjovat
2 CONC  Olavson in 1626. He left Skiftun in 1627. He lived also at Yrkje before he came to Lindanger. Three of Ola's sons, Jakob Sandvik, Bjørn and Per, the last in military service, wrote in 1673 a petition or a "bøneskriv" on some mone
2 CONC y they had borrowed from their brother Holger. The county magistrate promised them not to pursue lawsuit (only) if they could prove their right to the money (that means: Jacob , Bjørn and Per had to prove that it 
2 CONT
2 CONT was their money). 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married to Ingrid Jakobsdtr IKDAL.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2421. Ingrid Jakobsdtr IKDAL (1030) was born in 1600 in Ikdal, Tysvær, Rogaland, Norway. She was married first to Ola Holgerson and they had 6 children. After Ola's death in 1660, "widow" Ingrid married secondly to Per Eielson of 
2 CONC Nesheim in Sjernarøy who is listed as the next farmer of the half Lindanger farm after Ola. Children were: 
2 CONT
2 CONT  i. Torborg Olsdtr LINDANGER(1031) was born in 1620. She married Simon Jørgenson and lived in Sør Hidle and Aubø in Sjernarøy 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1194 ii. Holger Olson LINDANGER. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  iii. Jakob Olson LINDANGER(1032) was born in 1631. He married Berit (Brita) Olsdtr. and lived at Sandvik in Nedstrand. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  iv. Bjørn Olson LINDANGER/IKDAL(1033) was born in 1633. He died about 1698. He married Ingeborg Bårdsdtr from Aukland and was the farmer of the whole Bruk 1 (Dalen) farm at Ikdal. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  v. Ola Olson LINDANGER(1034) was born in 1640. He was mentioned in 1666. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  vi. Per Olson LINDANGER(1035). He was mentioned in 1673 in a family legal matter and it was indicated at this time that he was in the military.
2 CONT
2 CONT # 1729
2 CONT
2 CONT Lindanger (halve garden), Tysvær. Ola budde først på Skiftun i Hjelmeland 8, men flytta derifrå i 1627. Han budde så på Yrkje 7 før han kom til Lindanger. "Olluff" budde på Yrkje alt ikring 1630. I 1645 svara han koppskatt saman m
2 CONC ed kona si. Han budde her framleis i 1649. Det kan sjå ut til at Ingrid og andre mannen Per Eielson dreiv jord her ei tid. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Tre av sønene til Ola, Jakob Sandvik, Bjørn og Per, den siste i kongens teneste, skreiv i 1673 ein supplikk eller eit bøneskriv om nokre pengat dei hadde lånt av broren Holger. Amtmannen lova dei ikkje å forfølgja saka berre dei k
2 CONC unne prova retten sin til pengane.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT De bodde først på Skiftun, Hjelmeland, Rogaland. Han var bruker her sammen med broren Sjovat i 1626. De ble enige om at Ola skulle flytte fordi gården ikke var stor nok til 2 familier. De bodde så på Yrkje, Skjold, Tysvær, Rogalan
2 CONC d. Her er de nevnt i 1630, 1645 og 1649. Etter dette bodde de på Lindanger, Skjold, Tysvær, Rogaland. (Hjelmeland. Gard og folk, 1. Gardane på nordsida av Randøy, på Ombo, Jøsneset og i Jøsenfjorden. s. 173.) (Tysvær sokn. Gard og
2 CONC  ætt, 4. Skjoldastraumen. s. 462 og 544.)
