1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Soga om Vats page 594-595 Stokka (4a), (5), Ætt og Heim 1986 page 113-140 "Åsmunds-sønnene Johannes og Jon på Stokka og Nes".
2 CONT
2 CONT Se spesielt på side 131 i Ætt og Heim 1986.
2 CONT
2 CONT 8140. Johannes* ÅSMUNDSSON Stokka(867) (766)(827) (767) was born about 1590 in Viland gård #30, Vikedal, Rogaland, Norway. He was leased his father-in-law's farm in 1617 in Stokka gård #139, Vats, Rogaland, Norway. He died in 1658
2 CONC  in Stokka gård #139, Vats, Rogaland, Norway. Lensmann Johannes Osmundsson Stokka was a renowned and wealthy man, the wealthiest man and largest landowner in the entire skiprede. In 1645, Johannes had 5 farm hands and 8 female ser
2 CONC vants. He was the lensmann in Vikedal from 1612 to 1622. Folk traditions about him and his wife, Brynhild, have survived right up to the present day. 
2 CONT
2 CONT It is said that Johannes and Brynhild had 28 children. Only 9 are known to have reached adulthood. Interestingly enough, Johannes had to pay a fine of 61/2 dalar in 1610, because his eldest son was born very shortly after their we
2 CONC dding. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Johannes started out with 41/2 laupar smør in 1610, but by 1658 he owned about 44 laupar. Both his parents owned considerable property and since he was the only child of his mother, he inherited her entire estate. He divided his f
2 CONC ather's estate with two half-brothers, although one of these died without issue and he inherited half of his estate also. But Johannes was also a shrewd businessman and acquired a considerable amount of property in addition to wha
2 CONC t he inherited. He seems to have made a lot of money selling lumber to Scottish merchants. 
2 CONT
2 CONT There is a pew in the old church in Vats in which "Brønela Knudsdatter 1637" is carved and there is a rosemaled board in the church which has Johannes' seal on it. There is also a large painting hanging in the church believed to p
2 CONC ortray Johannes, Brynhild and their alleged 28 children. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The origins of Johannes' family has been the subject of a great deal of genealogical research and scholarly study. Based on an exhaustive study of original records concerning land transactions, inheritances and tax payments, Einar
2 CONC  Balle has made considerable progress in conclusively identifying the ancestors of Johannes. Mr Balle determined that Johannes' mother was the daughter of Arnbjørn Amundsson Ile and his father was Åsmund Eriksson Viland. Both appe
2 CONC ar to be descended from the ancient Norwegian noble families of Ingemund, Koll and Ænes. He was married to Brynhild* KNUTSDATTER Stokka in 1609 in Ryfylke, Rogaland, Norway.(640) (765)(640)
2 CONT
2 CONT 8141. Brynhild* KNUTSDATTER Stokka (868)(827) (767) was born about 1580 in Stokka gård #139, Vats, Rogaland, Norway. She was christened about 1581 in Vats, Rogaland, Norway.(640) She died in 1664 in Stokka gård #139, Vats, Rogalan
2 CONC d, Norway. 
2 CONT
